  inline because it genuinely cannot wait for that chunk: a bundled component
  script is a deferred ES module, so it runs AFTER the document is parsed —
  which is after first paint. Four things would visibly flash if this ran then:

    1. `--sidebar-reserve` drives `<main>`'s own left margin (BaseLayout.astro,
       see its comment), and ToolSidebar renders BEFORE `<main>` — a visitor
       who has hidden the rail would get the whole content column laid out at
       240px of reserve and then shifted to 0 (a real CLS hit, not a subtlety).
    2. `rail` transitions `transform 400ms` — restoring a hidden rail post-paint
       animates it sliding out on every page load instead of it simply never
       being there.
    3. A stored mode other than the server-rendered `defaultMode` would show
       the wrong category list first, then swap.
    4. A stored drag position would jump the rail vertically after paint.

